    _citation_year
    _citation_page_first
    _citation_page_last
    1 force-field    'J. Some Name'    10 12 2014 1 12
    2 software-code  'J. Another Name' 10 12 2014 1 12

  L.V. Correct citation to the publication of the original FF is of extreme
  importance. 

  S.G. I suggest using 'citation' category data items from the core
  CIF dictionary, and adding just a few TCOD relevant data items such
  as _tcod_citation_linkage that would show which part of the
  computation (force field, software code, etc.) does the paper
  describe. Other items should point, whenever possible, to
  machine-readable URLs with the force field or program code
  definitions (for software, this might be links to a source code for
  open source packages, links to a compiled binary packages for
  specific platform, the ones used in the computations, and yet
  another link would point to a web site describing the software (this
  is relevant for both open-source and proprietary programs).

;
_definition.update               2019-03-19
_definition.class                Datum
_type.container                  Single
_type.contents                   Text
_type.purpose                    State
_definition.id                   '_tcod_citation_linkage'
_name.object_id                  '_tcod_citation_linkage'
